        "text": "Ternary networks such as BitNet keep each weight as minus one, zero or plus one times a scale, so a multiply becomes an add, a subtract or nothing. gfternary.t27 fixes that scale at phi, about 1.618, and stores the three values in 2 bits: 00 is zero, 01 is plus phi, 10 is minus phi. Two bits have a fourth code, 11, and the spec folds it to zero instead of leaving it undefined. The spec also says what it does not claim: that a phi scale beats plain integer ternary weights is an open conjecture, and it names the measured gap that would falsify it. The player compiles it in your browser; most checks it cannot run here, and each skip says why.",
